    answer: "0.15 m behind the mirror",
    solutionSteps: ["[1 mark] For a convex mirror f = +0.3 m and u = -0.3 m. Mirror formula 1/v + 1/u = 1/f gives 1/v = 1/0.3 - (-1/0.3) = 2/0.3, so v = +0.15 m, i.e. the image is virtual, 0.15 m behind the mirror."],
